DEBUG_SAULO, temporary: when FFmpeg rejects an XMA frame, logs the context, input buffer, packet header, frame
position, whether the frame crossed into another packet or buffer, the loop data and whether guest memory changed
under the decoder. Only the first error of each kind (the message without its numbers) gets that line; the
10-second XMA summary counts the repeats. Also logs context work over 10 ms, XMADisableContext waits over 5 ms,
input starvation in that summary, and SDL callbacks that found the frame queue empty.

